  "solution": {
    "text": "Hydrogen peroxide oxidies lead sulphide to lead sulphate and itself gets reduced. Thus,  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>  acts as an oxidising agent in acidic medium.<br/><br/>Hydrogen peroxide reduces hypochlorous acid to chloride ion in acidic medium and itself gets oxidised.<br/><br/>Thus,  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>  acts as a reducing agent in acidic medium.",
